# lescall — Kamailio dispatcher backends (SIP signaling -> FreeSWITCH)
#
# Format:  setid  destination_uri  [flags] [priority] [attrs]
#
# setid 1 = "freeswitch media nodes". Today there is exactly ONE backend: the
# FreeSWITCH external profile on this same VM (private NIC 10.160.0.6:5080).
#
# >>> TO ADD A SECOND FREESWITCH NODE LATER (zero redesign): <<<
#   1. Append another line with the SAME setid (1) and the new node's IP:5080, e.g.
#        1 sip:10.160.0.7:5080
#   2. Run:  kamcmd dispatcher.reload
#   Dispatcher will load-balance/failover across all setid-1 nodes automatically
#   (algorithm set in kamailio.cfg). No restart, no config redesign.
#
# NOTE: when nodes live on OTHER hosts behind NAT, media relay (rtpengine) becomes
# necessary — see the rtpengine notes in kamailio.cfg.

1 sip:10.160.0.6:5080 0 0
